  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\nMuch cooler weather will arrive behind the cold front today as \n850 mb temperatures fall to around 6C. Starting to see some lake\neffect clouds develop downwind of Lake Erie early this morning,\nwith a few lake effect rain showers possible across the \nsnowbelt later this morning and afternoon. Even with the lake-\ninduced CAPE resulting from the near ~21C 850 mb/water \ntemperature difference, coverage should remain relatively \nlimited with a 700 mb inversion and dry air aloft in place. \nSlightly higher moisture arriving off of Lake Huron may result \nin better coverage of rain showers across portions of Northwest \nPennsylvania today. Given the chilly air mass in place and \ncloud cover, highs today may struggle to reach the 70 mark in \nsome spots. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...\nA large upper-level ridge across the Western and Central CONUS\nwill gradually expand further east into the Great Lakes by\nFriday into the weekend, resulting in temperatures to return\nnear or slightly above normal in the mid to upper 80s. However,\na series of upper-level troughs across Hudson Bay appear poised\nto block the eastward progression of the ridge. This pattern \nwould favor increasing rain chances across the area by early \nnext week (late Sunday through Tuesday), with the potential for\nsome organized stronger thunderstorms given the supportive mid \nand upper-level environment. Will continue to monitor trends \nover the next several days.",
